      "writtenOn": "2026-08-28T07:26:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "destroyResources() is only called during context shutdown/disconnect, so resetting it has not performance impact. Doing it upfront instead of during the destructor ensures child command buffers and framebuffers are destroyed before fResourceProvider.destroyResources() tears down the underlying pools, preventing internal pointers from temporarily dangling (which would otherwise require DanglingUntriaged annotations under MiraclePtr due to out-of-order destruction).",
